                            <comment id="15057999" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 15 Dec 2015 12:42:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Igor,&lt;br/&gt;
Please check if increment/decrement can be used as intrinsics as well: &lt;a href=&quot;https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/26td21ds.aspx&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/26td21ds.aspx&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15058135" author="isapego" created="Tue, 15 Dec 2015 14:34:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Vladimir,&lt;br/&gt;
We are using Visual Studio 2010 toolchain so we should look at this page instead: &lt;a href=&quot;https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/26td21ds(v=vs.100).aspx&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/26td21ds(v=vs.100).aspx&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
As you can see, 64-bit versions of atomic increment and decrement functions are not available in our case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also, I have added specific pragmas to be sure that intrinsics and not a functions are used.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15060102" author="skozlov" created="Wed, 16 Dec 2015 15:06:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Vasilisa, could you confirm that it&apos;s fixed and close?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15060535" author="vsidorova" created="Wed, 16 Dec 2015 18:56:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fix verified for Apache Ignite 1.5.0-b2 build #112. .Net examples still couldn&apos;t be executed but with another error. However it need additional investigation and problem statements&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
